WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.600
German poet Friedrich von Schiller once said,

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.610
"A courageous person thinks 
of themselves last."

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.490
I see.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.200
You're a courageous person, aren't you?

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.780
I didn't expect you'd come to see me.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.830
Recklessness is courage.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.040
In response to your feelings,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.300
I, Awaza Kodama, will sing just for you!

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.800
I'm counting on you, Single Gear!

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.050
Now, let it resound within you.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.030
Carve it into your soul!

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.950
His wounds aren't insignificant,

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.520
and he does have a fever,

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.290
but his life's in no danger.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.430
It's a result of getting hurt in the battle

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.920
and jumping into the water while exhausted.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.450
Not only was his body kept 
cold for several hours,

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.090
bacteria probably got in through the wound.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.680
We can make any number of guesses,

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.420
but we don't know for sure.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.940
At a time like this...

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.010
This is bad.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:57.440
Even though wounds sustained in the Ziggurat 
are greatly reduced upon returning here,

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.700
he took serious damage last time.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:04.830
For now, just think about getting better.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.720
Aren't I going to get worse?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.580
Am I just going to get better now?

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.960
No. Even thinking as positively as possible,

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.590
it's going to get worse.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.210
Then while I can still move...

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.210
Tazuna-kun,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.620
you can't fight like this.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:25.370
And if you do fight

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:28.220
it might kill you, even in the Ziggurat.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.600
The one whose life is at 
risk here is Koyori, right?

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.230
You know we can't escape 
that Hand Shaker, right?

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.470
The difference in our 
power is far too large,

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.150
and I'm wounded.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.030
Will they just sit back and do nothing when 
they've got an advantage like that?

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.660
I know I would finish them...

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:48.720
But...

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.790
If I lose, Koyori dies.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.160
Right?

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.180
I'm going to protect Koyori.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:56.920
No.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.930
Makihara-sensei!

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.380
It's true that, as you say,

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.930
your defeat will mean Koyori's death.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.920
But even so,

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.400
no.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.570
Why?

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:10.810
The odds are just too low.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.060
Tell me everything you know about your enemy.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:17.940
As a former Hand Shaker, I'll analyze them.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.690
I'll try and heal you, too.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.550
So...

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:22.950
All right.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:28.270
You're right. I wasn't thinking clearly.

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.110
I can't see myself winning now.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:30.870
I'll rest.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.730
Good.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.370
I promise good news.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.540
Get some sleep, Tazuna-kun.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.270
Makihara-sensei is too overconfident.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.460
Positive? Hah.

00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:00.520
He's just been optimistic and indecisive...

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:03.780
Does he really want to save you?

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.240
Don't worry.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.030
I'll protect you.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.080
Brother...

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:18.670
That isn't Takatsuki Musubu, your sister.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.210
It's true that yes,

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:24.170
at first you were a replacement for Musubu.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:28.930
I thought that I could never 
let go like I did with Musubu.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.550
But now it's different.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.760
I'll protect you, Koyori.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.940
I promise!

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.060
I'm the only one who can!

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.590
The fever medicine's working.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.400
I know where they are,

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.820
because she gave us her idol name.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.030
I was able to find them.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.010
Even if something happens to me,

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.710
I'll defeat those two.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.790
Koyori, let's go!

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:07.040
Tazuna?

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.470
You have to lie down.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:12.180
Makihara-sensei said you need rest.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:14.470
I have somewhere I have to go.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.730
Koyori-chan looks upset.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.260
It's for Koyori's sake.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:21.820
But...

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.610
Tazuna, lately you've 
been getting hurt a lot.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.360
Shut up! Leave me alone!

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:29.360
Tazuna!

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.990
Look at Koyori-chan's face

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.630
and tell me you're doing it for her sake.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.250
Shut up.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.210
Tazuna!

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.350
Tazuna, wait!

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:46.170
<i>No matter what Koyori thinks,</i>

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.930
<i>I have to win!</i>

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.790
So this is your world after all.

00:06:56.530 --> 00:07:01.150
But yesterday you fought here and lost.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:04.740
So this is the effect of my Nimrod?

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.150
It knows us?

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:08.750
Yes.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.910
But don't get the wrong idea.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.590
The reason I fought here last time

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:15.410
was because I wanted to win in your world.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.910
That won't change this time either.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.780
<i>First I'll destroy her Nimrod, 
which amplifies her power!</i>

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.430
Me?

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.850
<i>I'll defeat him before she can intervene!</i>

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:35.850
Oh, dear.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:41.540
Hey, I'm in the middle of one 
of Kodama-chan's concerts.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:46.200
It's true that you can leave 
the concert at any time, but...

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.400
That's a shame.

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:53.410
Hibiki-san, are you okay?

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.550
Yes, I'm all right!

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.210
Flash!

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:09.500
Damn it!

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.380
He's strong.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:14.060
Aww, no I'm not.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.640
I'm not strong at all.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.690
But my one job of being a manager,

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.730
and letting my idol's voice resound...

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:25.150
I take seriously!

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:36.700
Oh, no!

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:40.950
Of course Awaza Kodama's manager 
is going to be good at his job.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:44.260
Let the concert begin!

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:03.460
<i>I feel a different power than yesterday.</i>

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:08.270
<i>Her song and dance are amplifying 
her Nimrod's power even more.</i>

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.960
I can't lose...

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.700
I'll protect her...

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.170
I'll protect Koyori...

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.820
No matter what happens to me.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.070
Mahatma Gandhi once said

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:03.220
that strength doesn't come from the body,

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.580
it comes from an unbreakable will.

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:08.580
And that describes you to a T.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:09.980
But...

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.340
The concert's about to end.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.250
No encores.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.340
I won't let that happen...

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.850
Together...

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.360
I want to be...

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:38.030
with Tazuna...

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.320
Koyori?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:31.460
Koyori's Nimrod?

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:42.860
Kodama-chan!

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:44.760
I know!

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:48.410
I'll protect Tazuna.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.140
I'll stay with him.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.380
I see.

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:02.820
We're together.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:10.540
Will you fight with me, Koyori?

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.160
Yeah, Tazuna!

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:18.300
The two worlds aren't mixing...

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.260
But they're becoming one.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.050
Is this your Nimrod?

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:25.050
The gears are overlapping!

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:28.090
Kinda like a sprocket gear...

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.860
Sprocket... Gear.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.310
I bet that castle is Koyori's heart.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.390
Hibiki-san, now's not the 
time to be impressed.

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:39.180
That's right!

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.570
Oh, I'm done!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:42.570
Let it resound, Kodama-chan.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:43.930
Yeah.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:46.570
Now I've seen your power.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:49.160
I'll carve it into both of you!

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.040
If I'm with you, Tazuna, I can do it.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:57.040
Yeah.

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:08.810
My songs...

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:09.810
Kodama-chan!

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:27.290
<i>Gear skates... is this Koyori's power?</i>

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:29.240
<i>The power you gave me, Tazuna.</i>

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:35.350
<i>I was able to mesh with Tazuna!</i>

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.140
<i>They're behind me!</i>

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:43.560
We're meshing!

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:57.370
<i>They figured out how I move 
from the battles so far?</i>

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:58.190
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.540
I've come this far,

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.120
and won so many battles...

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.760
Awaza Kodama cannot leave this stage.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.100
Kodama-chan, no!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:18.620
I won't run.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:23.720
If I run, I, Awaza Kodama,

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:25.840
will cease to be Awaza Kodama!

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:28.780
To make our dreams come true,

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:31.600
I can't lose or run away.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:33.550
Let's go, Koyori!

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:35.220
Yeah, Tazuna!

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:51.240
My... my dream...

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:53.260
No...

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.140
It's over...

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.890
You lost, that's all, right?

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.640
I lost!

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.500
I lost...

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:29.430
It's over...

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:33.530
No! It was over a long time ago!

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.500
My songs are for all my fans?

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:43.060
Who are my fans? Where are they?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.260
Opinions on my concerts?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.040
<b>#ThingsYourIconsWouldSay
Iyaben Rabbit Cafe Weird Ham
Following 260 Followers 6</b>

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.040
<b>Awaza Kodama</b>

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.820
I searched online and
 nobody said a thing!

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:51.050
Because of that president, I've barely 
got access to any concert halls.

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:54.680
If I'd known this was going to happen, 
I would've taken him up on his offer!

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:57.180
I would've given up on the name Awaza Kodama,

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:02.380
and been used and thrown away under 
some weird name at his company,

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:04.060
and I still would've had more of a chance.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.520
But I...

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:11.990
<b>Mahatma Gandhi
"Strength doesn't come from the body.
It comes from an unbreakable will."
28th American President
Thomas Woodrow Wilson
"There are no coincidences in fate. Before humans 
encounter a particular fate, they make it for themselves."
French Emperor Napoleon Bonaparte
"Do not fear ignorance. Fear false knowledge."</b>

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:11.920
Awaza Kodama's just a fake anyway!

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:16.200
Her songs, her words, everything! Everything!

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.360
<b>Russian author Maxim Gorky
"Talent is believing in 
yourself, and your own power!"
French author Antoine Prévost
"Time can be gold or lead, 
depending on how you use it."</b>

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.360
<b>My favorite quotes
Use them if you like!</b>

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:18.680
It's the same with me being a Hand Shaker!

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.980
I know that!

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:27.840
The reason I was able to win so far was 
because you picked my opponents, wasn't it?

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:30.590
You knew?

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:31.840
I know.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.300
You were working with that doctor.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.480
You promised not to fight each other,

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.670
and to exchange information,

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:42.730
avoiding opponents who'd have 
an advantage against us

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:46.730
and choosing opponents even I could beat.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:51.060
Otherwise someone like me 
would've lost a long time ago.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:57.790
I didn't fight them because they didn't 
want to fight you, Kodama-chan.

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:01.480
Otherwise they would've 
come after us earlier.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:02.670
That's who they...

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:03.500
Shut up!

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.300
Either way, I lost.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.500
It's over now.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.630
You really are a fool.

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:14.120
You did all this for a girl 
who can't do anything and

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.970
bought into my delusions 
about being an idol.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.260
You even quit your job...

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:23.020
You threw your whole life 
into the mud for me!

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:40.910
You're right.

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:43.560
It is in the mud.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.420
But that's nothing new, Kodama-chan.

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:53.350
We never won at anything, did we?

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:57.180
We're just an underground 
idol and her manager.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.160
So we're in the mud.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.180
You can't get arrogant about it,

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.600
but I believe in you.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:08.620
We lost in the Ziggurat,

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:11.720
but even if we don't borrow 
power from God there

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.730
and try to make our dreams 
come true that way,

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:16.940
my dream will come true, Kodama-chan.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:18.280
Why?

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.780
Because you're Awaza Kodama-chan.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:25.620
You are my dream.

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:30.000
Otherwise I wouldn't have 
stopped being your fan,

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.170
which had been the goal of my life,

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.870
and become your manager.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:40.380
I wouldn't have let my whole life 
revolve a girl younger than me,

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:42.260
who I'm not in love with.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.010
Kodama-chan...

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.920
Kodama-chan, you do have a fan.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:00.890
Do you need the help of a manager?

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:06.910
Just for this one moment...

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:11.050
Even when I sing in town, 
nobody listens to me.

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:13.900
Even though I barely have any fans, or jobs...

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:18.550
You really are a fool, Hibiki-san.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:26.560
But that's what makes you Awaza 
Kodama's skilled manager!

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:29.230
I was prepared to reluctantly retire

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.420
and go back to being a normal girl, but...

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:39.340
If my fans, and my manager, 
want me to stay I guess I will.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:43.210
Okay, go make my dream come true.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:46.080
I'll send the two of them a pair of tickets,

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:51.950
and shake their hands and make them 
understand what an amazing idol they got

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.580
to hear up close.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:56.440
So what's our next job?

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:02.020
Sun Tzu said that the art 
of war is all about speed.

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:03.400
Huh?

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:04.600
Is that right...

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:05.720
Um...

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:08.220
Anyway, time is important!

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.820
Kodama-chan!

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:12.590
That's my Kodama-chan!

00:20:12.590 --> 00:20:13.850
It's resounding within me,

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:16.300
since my name's Hibiki.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:18.080
I've been meaning to say this for a while,

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:20.020
but I'm pretty sure that's not why.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:22.730
Oh, right.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:24.590
That concert that got canceled...

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:27.740
Can you leave your schedule open?

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:28.890
But...

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:31.690
I got an appointment with President Nabeta.

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:34.520
Hibiki-san, that won't...

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:38.030
No, let's try it.

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:40.620
Nothing is impossible for Awaza Kodama.

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.240
That's my Kodama-chan!

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:43.800
Your self-confidence resounds within me,

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:44.800
because I'm Hibiki.

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:55.350
Koyori, I'm really sorry.

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:58.840
We won thanks to you.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:02.040
I couldn't do anything on my own.

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:06.760
But I ran ahead on my own...

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:11.450
I was so convinced I had to do something.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.460
You always protected me.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:21.640
Thank you,

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:25.580
for being with me.

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:32.970
You, too...

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:36.230
Thanks for being with me.

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:12.410
<i>Koyori's world expanded.</i>

00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:15.930
<i>Amidst a peace where they 
are blessed together,</i>

00:23:15.930 --> 00:23:18.230
<i>the young man looks up at the sky and asks,</i>

00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:21.920
<i>"If I ever could let go of this hand,</i>

00:23:22.470 --> 00:23:23.800
<i>what would happen then?"</i>

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:27.130
<i>The girl looks down at their clasped hands</i>

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:28.670
<i>and answers with a sigh.</i>

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:34.780
<i>Next time on Hand Shakers, 
Episode 10: Kitten Kitchen.</i>

00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:39.100
<i>Their trial isn't over yet.</i>
